From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:35:22 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dt-bindings: cirrus,cs42l84: Reference dai-common.yaml

The Apple device trees give the CS42L84 headphone jack codec a
sound-name-prefix, which ASoC puts in front of the codec's control and
widget names. That property is described in dai-common.yaml, which this
binding does not reference, and with additionalProperties set to false
the binding rejects it on every CS42L84 machine.

Reference dai-common.yaml and use unevaluatedProperties, as the CS42L42
and CS42L43 bindings do.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
(cherry picked from commit 7556a8ca8e09034a816cf5a70d7027f8f3c8f77c)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cirrus,cs42l84.yaml | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cirrus,cs42l84.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cirrus,cs42l84.yaml
index 7f8338e8ae..4c376062d6 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cirrus,cs42l84.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cirrus,cs42l84.yaml
@@ -36,7 +36,10 @@ required:
   - compatible
   - reg
 
-additionalProperties: false
+allOf:
+  - $ref: dai-common.yaml#
+
+unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 examples:
   - |
